# chart_app Cursor rules

Read `chart_app/docs/VIEW_STATE.md` and `chart_app/docs/DECISIONS.md` before
changing view, overlays, replay, or live WS.

## Never touch

- `backend/` (live options bot) — read-only from chart work
- `.env` (API keys)
- Strategy **signal logic** in `backtest/` — chart imports it. Do not copy,
  fork, or “simplify” detect_swings / collect_signals / RSI div into
  `chart_app/`. Overlay is display + the same functions (parity).

## Time on the chart

- Every new series / overlay / marker / live candle **time** must go through
  `snapToGrid` and must not exceed the last candle (`capToLastCandle`).
- Call `assertGrid`. Off-grid times = phantom LWC indices.
- Do not insert dummy `t-1` points to break a line (VWAP uses extra series).

## View / camera

- Time scale owner is `chart_app/static/view.js`. Other files use
  `view.request(...)`.
- Do **not** add `setVisibleRange` or `applyOptions({ timeScale: { rightOffset } })`
  in new code. Allowed `rightOffset` spots only (see VIEW_STATE.md): chart
  create, `jump-live` / `scrollLive` in `view.js`.
- Camera is **logical**: `setVisibleLogicalRange`. Future pad =
  `lastIndex + (t - lastTime) / barSec`.

## Server

- Heavy CPU (overlay, indicators, gzip cache) → `asyncio.to_thread`.
- Delta REST only through `chart_app/delta_rest.py` (cap 2, 429 backoff,
  disk cache). Do not add raw `httpx`/`requests` to Delta from other modules.

## Commit gate

- After a chart_app behavior change: e2e **fixtures** (`python chart_app/tests/run_e2e.py`)
  must pass, then `--live` if the change touches live WS / last-bar follow.
- Do not commit failing fixtures. Do not `git add -A` (leave unrelated dirty
  files). Do not revert in-progress `view.js` / `app.js` / e2e work unless
  the task says so.
